From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: N-PHY: enable the BCM43217 external PAs

On the BCM43217 the external PAs of the two cores are enabled in PMU chip
control register 1: bit 13 for core 0 and bit 8 for core 1, as Broadcom's
CCTRL43217_EXTPA_C0/C1. b43 and bcma never set them. After a power-on
they are clear, the PAs stay off and TX power control cannot reach its
target: on an ASUS RT-AC56U (BCM43217, extpagain2g 3) the power index
ends at 0x30 against 0x50, the estimate at 0x030 against 0x350, a phone
sees the AP 17 dB weaker and TCP download is 3 Mbit/s.

The vendor driver sets both bits, read back after it ran, and they stay
set over a warm reboot, which hid this whenever b43 was loaded after it.
With them cleared by hand b43 runs as after a power-on; set, it runs as
after the vendor driver.

Set them at N-PHY init on a BCM43217 whose 2.4 GHz PA is external.

Signed-off-by: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
@@ -7103,6 +7103,18 @@ static int b43_phy_initn(struct b43_wlde
 #endif
 		}
 	}
+#ifdef CPTCFG_B43_BCMA
+	/*
+	 * The BCM43217 enables the external PAs of its two cores in PMU chip
+	 * control register 1, bit 13 for core 0 and bit 8 for core 1. Nothing
+	 * else sets them: after a power-on they are clear, the PAs stay off
+	 * and TX power control runs open, at a fraction of the power.
+	 */
+	if (dev->dev->bus_type == B43_BUS_BCMA &&
+	    dev->dev->chip_id == BCMA_CHIP_ID_BCM43217 && !b43_nphy_ipa(dev))
+		bcma_chipco_chipctl_maskset(&dev->dev->bdev->bus->drv_cc, 1,
+					    ~0, BIT(13) | BIT(8));
+#endif
 	nphy->use_int_tx_iq_lo_cal = b43_nphy_ipa(dev) ||
 		phy->rev >= 7 ||
 		(phy->rev >= 5 &&
